#
# Everything from here on is written one command per line rather
# than chained with periods. A chained "a. b. c" line is handed to
# the game as a single buffered input, which changes when the
# jester's random-event daemon gets a chance to fire compared to
# each command arriving as its own read -- enough to actually change
# outcomes (a chained six-move stretch here once triggered a bat
# abduction that a separated version of the same six moves did not).
# Since this section leans on that daemon firing at specific,
# verified moments (the alligator turn below, in particular), each
# command gets its own line.

