# Double Fanucci is a raw single-keystroke UI, like the Tower of Bozbar
# and Peggleboz: each play is chosen by moving a cursor with U/D/L/R
# (down moves within a column, right moves a column over, both
# wrapping) and selecting with a bare keystroke for Enter -- written
# here as ">" per the acceptance-script format, same as the picture
# dismissals elsewhere. Navigating with anything else (a whole word,
# say) feeds the menu one raw character at a time and can walk it
# somewhere nonsensical.
#
# The actual win condition, from the source (HIGHWAY.ZIL): the very
# first UNDERTRUMP played right after the jester discards Trebled
# Fromps sets a hidden streak counter to 1 if the card is one the
# scoring table allows for that play (most are); two more UNDERTRUMPs
# in a row, each independently valid, complete the streak and win
# outright. Any other play in between -- even a harmless DRAW -- or a
# single invalid UNDERTRUMP resets the streak to zero, so the run below
# discards the whole starting hand (revealing what it holds) and
# redraws until all three hand slots hold cards confirmed valid for
# UNDERTRUMP, then just draws (which never touches the streak) until
# the jester's discard naturally happens, and fires all three
# undertrumps back to back.
#
# This makes this accept script fragile to change: it hinges on
# the seed dealing three specific replacement cards (an Eight of
# Fromps, a Four of Faces, and, by luck, an already-valid Trebled
# Fromps drawn along the way) and on the discard landing at exactly
# the twelfth stall draw. A different seed will deal different cards
# and need different stalling, though the shape of the approach -- vet
# the hand while it's safe to, then wait -- carries over.

